# Interaction latency, part 3 of 3: scroll.
#
# Its own script because it needs a transcript long enough to scroll. Every
# hand-written thread in the mock fits on screen at 1100x760, so a scroll arm
# on one of those settles never -- a fixture that proves nothing rather than a
# fast app. The 120-turn perf fixture is the one place there is something to
# scroll.
#
# Measured to `jump_to_bottom`, the affordance the app draws only once the view
# has left the bottom. It is ink that scrolling creates, so it cannot be
# confused with the always-present scroll container.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_BIG_TRANSCRIPT=1 HANABI_OPEN=rbig

require_thread rbig
mouse_move 650 400
wait_frames 12

watch_ink scroll ui jump_to_bottom
scroll_wheel 0 3
wait_frames 25
expect_latency scroll 8
